  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The function f is defined by f(x) = 2x² − 3. (d) Write an expression for f(a). (e) Write an expression for f(a + 1). (f) Simplify f(a + 1) − f(a)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Substituting into a function means replacing every x in the rule by whatever is inside the brackets."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p120_q02.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p120-q02 from workbook page 120."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Replace x by a in f(x) = 2x² − 3.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Direct substitution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f(a) = 2a² − 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Replace x by (a + 1), keeping the bracket.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "f(a + 1) = 2(a + 1)² − 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f(a + 1) = 2(a + 1)² − 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Expand and simplify.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(a + 1)² = a² + 2a + 1, so 2(a² + 2a + 1) − 3 = 2a² + 4a + 2 − 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: f(a + 1) = 2a² + 4a − 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Subtract f(a) from f(a + 1), using a bracket around f(a).",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "(2a² + 4a − 1) − (2a² − 3) = 2a² + 4a − 1 − 2a² + 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 4a + 2"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Replace x by a and then by (a + 1) in the rule 2x² − 3, expand the second one, and subtract."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(d) f(a) = 2a² − 3  (e) f(a + 1) = 2a² + 4a − 1  (f) f(a + 1) − f(a) = 4a + 2"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Function notation is an instruction to substitute: whatever sits inside the brackets takes the place of every x in the rule. Because both expressions contain the same 2a² term, subtracting cancels the quadratic part and leaves a linear expression — this difference, 4a + 2, measures how much the function grows over a step of one unit."
    }
  ],
